<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aller</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aller is a river in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, about 260 kilometres long, a right tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a>. It rises near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a> and flows north-west through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, past Wolfsburg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celle">Celle</a>, to join the Weser near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verden">Verden</a>. Its valley formed the heartland of the Welf duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a>, whose dukes resided at Celle.</p></div>
